    {
      "number": 41,
      "title": "Decision: Where should Burrow keep its cache?",
      "url": "https://github.com/fixture-owner/fixture-repo/issues/41",
      "state": "OPEN",
      "labels": [
        {
          "id": "LA_fixture_decision",
          "name": "decision",
          "description": "A major design decision that waits on Mark",
          "color": "FFCC3D"
        }
      ],
      "author": {
        "id": "U_markhazlewood42",
        "is_bot": false,
        "login": "markhazlewood42",
        "name": ""
      },
      "body": "## Question\n\nWhere should Burrow keep its cache folder?\n\n## Context\n\nThe cache is the only part of the storage that grows without a limit. Today it sits in the data folder, so a backup of the data folder saves the cache too.\n\n## Options\n\n- A: Keep it in the data folder. Nothing changes for users, and backups stay large.\n- B: Move it to the temp folder of the operating system. Backups shrink, and the cache is lost at a restart.\n- C: Move it to a new `cache` folder next to the data folder. Backups can skip it, and the installer must move old caches once.\n\n## Recommendation\n\nC: it keeps the cache over a restart and lets a backup skip it.\n\n## Docs\n\n- docs/guides/setup.md#storage\n- docs/guides/setup.md#first-run\n- docs/guides/setup.md#no-such-heading\n\n## Raised by\n\nSession fixture-session-1, branch `feature/cache-folder`.\n\n## Waits on this\n\nThe cache change in PR 12.\n",
      "comments": [],
      "createdAt": "2026-10-05T10:00:00Z",
      "updatedAt": "2026-10-05T10:00:00Z",
